course: dictionary
lesson: 15181
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them tells you which one you need. «The pond was green and scummy after the hot summer.» The clues are green and pond. Scum is a dirty layer floating on water, so scummy means covered with that dirty layer.
explain: «It was a scummy trick to take Sam's turn.» Nobody is talking about dirt here. The clue is taking a turn that was not fair. Scummy can be a rude, slang word for nasty or dishonest.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «the pond was covered with a dirty layer» still make sense? Does «it was a dishonest trick» still make sense? The meaning that fits is the right one.
fact: Scummy is an adjective, so it describes a noun: scummy, scummier, scummiest.
fact: «Scummy» means covered with scum, a dirty layer floating on liquid.
fact: «Scummy» can also be slang, meaning nasty, dirty or dishonest.
fact: Common phrases are «scummy water» and «a scummy thing to do».
fact: The sentence around a word is its context, and context shows you which meaning is meant.
exercise: «The bath had a scummy ring round the edge.» What does scummy mean here? | Cold and wet | Shiny and clean | *Covered with a dirty layer of scum | Full of bubbles
exercise: «Hiding the ball and blaming Kai was a scummy thing to do.» What does scummy mean in this sentence? | Loud and cheerful | *Nasty and dishonest | Covered in ice | Very tall
exercise: Which word completes this sentence? «The green pond was ___ than the clean lake.» | scummiest | scummy | *scummier | scum
test: «Ben said the pond looked scummy, so he did not swim.» What does scummy mean here? | Warm and sunny | Deep and blue | Cool and quiet | *Covered with a dirty layer on top of the water
test: «Taking the prize he did not win was a scummy trick.» What does scummy mean? | *Nasty and dishonest | Very tired | Shiny and new | Bright and silly
exam: Which sentence uses scummy to mean nasty or dishonest? | The pond had a scummy top layer | The scummy water was cold | *He told a scummy lie to get out of the chores | The bath was scummy with soap
